From 1457449c25b5cd558ff23bac86dff6a023ab3692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OLS-cPanel-WHM <2tdv@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Apply the ModSecurity ctl:ruleRemove* value fix to v3.0.15

OWASP CRS 3.3.10 (cPanel's OWASP3 vendor) uses
ctl:ruleRemoveTargetByTag=<tag>;XML://@* in rule 901181; libmodsecurity
v3.0.15 refuses '@' there and the whole rule set fails to load. The
patch is the upstream fix (v3/master 28f6c0782c51, 497df63d42d4) with
the generated scanner.
---
 script/build_libmodsec.sh                     |    1 +
 .../olscp-modsecurity-ctl-remove-values.patch | 6804 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 6805 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 script/olscp-modsecurity-ctl-remove-values.patch

diff --git a/script/build_libmodsec.sh b/script/build_libmodsec.sh
index b08a759..17cc8f8 100755
--- a/script/build_libmodsec.sh
+++ b/script/build_libmodsec.sh
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ git reset --hard
 git checkout -b v3/master origin/v3/master
 git pull
 git checkout v3.0.15
+git apply ../../script/olscp-modsecurity-ctl-remove-values.patch
 
 export PATH=/home/build/tools/bin/:$PATH
 sh build.sh
diff --git a/script/olscp-modsecurity-ctl-remove-values.patch b/script/olscp-modsecurity-ctl-remove-values.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9eeec37
--- /dev/null
+++ b/script/olscp-modsecurity-ctl-remove-values.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,6804 @@
+From 3ca57e2168482365b8203fa189e086f6a20c2483 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: OLS-cPanel-WHM <2tdv@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] Accept '@', '=', '(', ')' and quotes in ctl:ruleRemove*
+ values
+
+Backport of upstream v3/master 28f6c0782c51 (#3565) and 497df63d42d4 to
+v3.0.15, with src/parser/seclang-scanner.cc regenerated by flex 2.6.4
+(the committed scanner reproduces byte for byte from the unpatched .ll).
+
+OWASP CRS 3.3.10 rule 901181 removes XML attribute targets with
+ctl:ruleRemoveTargetByTag=<tag>;XML://@*; v3.0.15 refuses to load it
+("Expecting an action, got: @*"), so the whole rule set fails.
